# 1. Node.js Seed Script Path Error

## Problem

While attempting to seed the MongoDB database, the following error occurred:

```bash
Error: Cannot find module '/home/ubuntu/se-sparta-test-app/se-sparta-test-app/app/seeds/seed.js'
```

## Cause

The command incorrectly duplicated the project directory path while already inside the repository directory.

Incorrect command:

```bash
nodejs se-sparta-test-app/app/seeds/seed.js
```

## Solution

Used the correct relative path:

```bash
nodejs app/seeds/seed.js
```

Or absolute path:

```bash
nodejs /home/ubuntu/se-sparta-test-app/app/seeds/seed.js
```

## What I Learned

* Importance of understanding Linux file paths
* Relative vs absolute paths
* Debugging Node.js module errors

