# 2. MongoDB Remote Connection Failure

## Problem

The application server could not connect to MongoDB remotely.

## Cause

MongoDB was configured to only accept local connections:

```bash
bindIp: 127.0.0.1
```

## Solution

Updated MongoDB configuration file:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/mongod.conf
```

Changed:

```bash
bindIp: 0.0.0.0
```

Restarted MongoDB:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart mongod
```

## What I Learned

* Importance of network binding
* MongoDB remote access configuration
* Security considerations when exposing services

