# 4. Nginx Reverse Proxy Issues

## Problem

Users had to access the application using:

```bash
APP_IP:3000
```

instead of standard HTTP traffic on port 80.

## Cause

Nginx reverse proxy was not configured.

## Solution

Modified Nginx configuration:

```bash
sudo sed -i '51c\proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;' /etc/nginx/sites-available/default
```

Restarted Nginx:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

## What I Learned

* Reverse proxy architecture
* Role of Nginx in production deployments
* Traffic forwarding concepts

